--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1 - Check multicast traffic is forwarded when the static IGMP group is configured
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4# show ip igmp groups                       <- baseline: empty

u4(config)# interface vlan10
u4(config-if)# ip igmp static-group 239.4.4.4 interface port1.0.2

u4# show ip igmp groups
IGMP Connected Group Membership
Group Address    Interface            Uptime   Expires  Last Reporter
239.4.4.4        vlan10               00:00:05  stopped 0.0.0.0

u4# show ip igmp groups 239.4.4.4 detail
Interface:      vlan10
Group:          239.4.4.4
Flags:          SG
Uptime:         00:00:06
Group mode:     Exclude (Static)
Last reporter:  0.0.0.0
Source list is empty
  => Group registered STATICALLY (Flags SG, mode "Exclude (Static)", Expires "stopped",
     no reporter). No host join was sent.

u5# ping 239.4.4.4 source 10.10.10.3 repeat 30 interval 1
--- 239.4.4.4 ping statistics ---
30 packets transmitted, 0 received, 100% packet loss, time 30198ms
host# tcpdump host 239.4.4.4 => 30 frames of 30 sent (0.0% loss)
   IP 10.10.10.3 > 239.4.4.4: ICMP echo request, id 14059, seq 1, length 64
   IP 10.10.10.3 > 239.4.4.4: ICMP echo request, id 14059, seq 2, length 64
   IP 10.10.10.3 > 239.4.4.4: ICMP echo request, id 14059, seq 3, length 64
  => 30/30 forwarded to the host with 0% loss, purely on the static group.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2 - Leave traffic running (membership maintained)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4# show ip igmp groups 239.4.4.4 detail   (after soak)
Group:          239.4.4.4
Flags:          SG
Uptime:         00:00:49
Group mode:     Exclude (Static)
  => static membership persists unchanged (never ages).  SCOPE: 30 s / 1 pps sample.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 3 - Remove static IGMP group configuration  (stream stops, tables clear)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4(config-if)# no ip igmp static-group 239.4.4.4 interface port1.0.2

u4# show ip igmp groups
                                             <- group cleared

u5# ping 239.4.4.4 source 10.10.10.3 repeat 5 interval 1   (after removal)
--- 239.4.4.4 ping statistics ---
5 packets transmitted, 0 received, 100% packet loss, time 4133ms
host# after removal => 1 frames received (expect 0)
